- When authoring new Terraform modules, optimize for these qualities

- Single Responsibility Principle
- Highly re-usable and generic
- Always include inline explanatory code comments 
- Always validate variables and make sure they have clear descriptions
- Always use consistent naming conventions for everything. When it becomes necessary to invent new naming conventions, do so, but make sure to keep NAMING_CONVENTIONS.md updated with whatever changes you make
- Always write tests for modules and make sure they pass.  We also need to make sure terragrunt init and terragrunt plan succeed.
- If you don't have Azure credentials, use the command az login to authenticate with Azure.
- Always user the latest versions of Terraform, Terraform Providers, and tools generally.  As of writing the latest version of the AzureRM provider is 4.23.0.